# Lotka and Volterra: rabbits x and foxes y.
#   x' = ax - bxy,   y' = -cy + dxy,
# with a = 1, b = .1, c = 1.5, d = .075, from 10 rabbits and 5 foxes. The
# numbers go round a closed cycle: the rabbits rise, the foxes follow, the
# rabbits fall. One cycle takes a little over 5 units of time.
    t = 0,
    h = 0.05,
    a = 1, b = .1, c = 1.5, d = .075,
    x = 10,
    y = 5,
1   PRINT t, x, y.
    n = 0,
2   Dx = ax - bxy,
    Dy = -cy + dxy,
    n = n + 1,
    e = n - 9.5,
    CP 2,
    e = t - 11.75,
    CP 1,
    STOP
